WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.668 line:0%
-My first guest
is an Oscar winner

00:00:02.668 --> 00:00:04.504 line:0%
starring alongside
Denzel Washington and Jared Leto

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:08.808 line:0%
in -- in the new film
"The Little Things,"

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:12.245 line:0%
which will be in theaters
this Friday and on HBO Max.

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:15.382 line:0%
Here is Rami Malek.
-What up, baby?!

00:00:15.382 --> 00:00:18.284
-Rami Malek, hello and welcome
back to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:20.987
You're looking fantastic.
Look at this look.

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:23.856
You're pulling it off again.
Another look.

00:00:23.856 --> 00:00:25.991
-I'm pulling off
another look, man.

00:00:25.991 --> 00:00:28.594
-You know what's so weird?
Like, now -- I have kids now,

00:00:28.594 --> 00:00:31.464
and I've never seen the
"Night at the Museum" movies.

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:36.069
And here you walk in,
and I go, "What?! What?!"

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:37.503
-Dude.

00:00:37.503 --> 00:00:39.672
-It's the biggest thing.
My kids love you.

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:42.008
-Oh, Frannie and Winnie.
Give them my love.

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:44.110
-Yeah, dude. Exactly.
Oh, my gosh.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:46.145
-The best part
of that experience

00:00:46.145 --> 00:00:49.415
was, you know,
Ben was great to me.

00:00:49.415 --> 00:00:51.151
-Yeah. Good.

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:53.486
-I'll tell you something
that nobody really knows,

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:59.325
is I was playing that role
so camp at first.

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:01.594
Maybe not "camp"
is the right word,

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:02.895
but I was going for it.

00:01:02.895 --> 00:01:06.198
This guy was supposed to be
in a sarcophagus

00:01:06.198 --> 00:01:09.669
at Cambridge University,
and I popped out of that coffin

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:12.404
and I played it
like a British dandy,

00:01:12.404 --> 00:01:14.840
and the studio was like,
"Nuh-unh!"

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:17.009
-Did you really?
-And so -- Yeah.

00:01:17.009 --> 00:01:21.914
And so I went back
to Los Angeles from Canada,

00:01:21.914 --> 00:01:25.285
and I'm like, "I don't think
that went very well."

00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:30.423
But Stiller and I got along
exceptionally well.

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:34.260
And he was laughing at a few
ad libs that I was throwing out,

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:36.395
so I was like,
"Something's telling me

00:01:36.395 --> 00:01:38.097
that some part
of this went right,

00:01:38.097 --> 00:01:40.333
but some part of it
went horribly wrong."

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:42.235
-Wow.
-'Cause I feel uncomfortable.

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:44.437
They're calling me back
for a makeup test.

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:45.872
My agent calls me and goes,

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:49.141
"There's a breakdown coming out
for this role again."

00:01:49.141 --> 00:01:50.743
So I was like,
"I'm getting fired."

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:53.112
-That's not good.

00:01:53.112 --> 00:01:57.249
-The only reason that I got back
and had to re-audition

00:01:57.249 --> 00:02:00.052
was because Stiller said,

00:02:00.052 --> 00:02:02.421
"Nah. I think you guys
are making a mistake here."

00:02:02.421 --> 00:02:05.357
So that was one
super-cool thing.

00:02:05.357 --> 00:02:09.629
The other great thing
was Robin Williams

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:12.165
for, you know, three movies --
-Yeah.

00:02:12.165 --> 00:02:14.800
-And, sad,
but on the third one,

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:18.304
we're shooting
at the British Museum at night,

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:20.706
and we have the place
all to ourselves.

00:02:20.706 --> 00:02:22.775
And Robin --
you could tell something

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:24.277
was happening with him, right?

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:27.780
He had -- He would go on these
riffs every once in a while

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:30.016
and light up the world,
and you'd be like,

00:02:30.016 --> 00:02:33.052
"Oh, my God. Who are you?"
-"Who is this?"

00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:36.022
-And then dip back down
into this other place.

00:02:36.022 --> 00:02:38.758
He'd see us all
on our phones and devices,

00:02:38.758 --> 00:02:40.126
and he'd be like,

00:02:40.126 --> 00:02:42.228
"What happened to this?
What happened to this?"

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:45.564
And so I see him kind of veer
off, and he walks off alone,

00:02:45.564 --> 00:02:48.967
and he's just kind of staring
at this massive rock

00:02:48.967 --> 00:02:50.536
in the British Museum.

00:02:50.536 --> 00:02:52.839
And I'm like, "Oh, man.

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:55.541
What's going on with him?
Is he all right?"

00:02:55.541 --> 00:02:58.944
So I walk up to kind of say,
"Is everything okay?"

00:02:58.944 --> 00:03:00.680
And he looks at me,

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:03.750
just kind of slightly
over the shoulder, and he goes,

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:07.153
"How often do you get to be
alone with the Rosetta Stone?"

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:11.957
-[Stammers]

00:03:11.957 --> 00:03:14.560
That's the best story
I've ever heard in my life.

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:17.129
-Amazing right?
-Wow!

00:03:17.129 --> 00:03:19.065
And you were like,
"Apparently not enough

00:03:19.065 --> 00:03:21.300
because I just interrupted you."

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:24.370
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:27.173
-It was so good.
-I always love talking to you.

00:03:27.173 --> 00:03:30.276
The last time I talked to you,
we were at the Time 100.

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:33.379
And I don't know
if you remember. It was --

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:37.316
I mean, it was --
Every cool person was there.

00:03:37.316 --> 00:03:40.686
It was actually
a really great night.

00:03:40.686 --> 00:03:42.120
Nancy Pelosi --

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:44.590
You and I and Nancy Pelosi
hung out and took a photo.

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:46.859
-Well, yeah.
-Look at this.

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:49.195
Look how tan I was.

00:03:49.195 --> 00:03:51.964
-It was so cool to hang out
with you there and her there.

00:03:51.964 --> 00:03:54.533
And, you know, she was a fan
of "Bohemian Rhapsody."

00:03:54.533 --> 00:03:57.236
I was like, "Well,
I'm a fan of you, Nancy."

00:03:57.236 --> 00:03:59.304
-Yeah.
-But she dug the movie,

00:03:59.304 --> 00:04:00.806
which was cool.

00:04:00.806 --> 00:04:05.278
-You went on to win the Oscar.
You won the Academy Award.

00:04:05.278 --> 00:04:09.781
-It was such a trip, man.
It was such a trip.

00:04:09.781 --> 00:04:14.086
The coolest part is --
We had to keep it under wraps,

00:04:14.086 --> 00:04:18.258
but Queen opened that night,
if you remember.

00:04:18.258 --> 00:04:20.959
-Yes.
-And so you hear that music --

00:04:20.959 --> 00:04:22.462
And because, you know,

00:04:22.462 --> 00:04:25.097
I've spent almost two years
preparing for it --

00:04:25.097 --> 00:04:27.633
I'm kind of instantly
brought back

00:04:27.633 --> 00:04:31.303
to the first moment
of acknowledging

00:04:31.303 --> 00:04:34.273
that I might play this man
and what that meant,

00:04:34.273 --> 00:04:37.209
and so the whole thing
kind of came full circle,

00:04:37.209 --> 00:04:39.545
and I had my mom there
and my brother and sister...

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:40.813
-No!

00:04:40.813 --> 00:04:43.116
-So, for me, it's --
The statue is everything.

00:04:43.116 --> 00:04:44.984
The experience just kind of

00:04:44.984 --> 00:04:47.653
was overwhelming
for so many reasons.

00:04:47.653 --> 00:04:50.022
Speaking of Mom, on Friday,

00:04:50.022 --> 00:04:52.191
she's got
a very special birthday.

00:04:52.191 --> 00:04:56.028
So, I love you, lady.
Happy birthday.

00:04:56.028 --> 00:04:58.430
-Aww. Mom, we love you.

00:04:58.430 --> 00:05:00.599
Look what you made.
What a great kid.

00:05:00.599 --> 00:05:03.168
Look what you did.
Look what you made.

00:05:03.168 --> 00:05:06.172
Brought into the world.
How cool is this guy?

00:05:06.172 --> 00:05:11.377
-And to piggyback off of family,
I mean, you guys --

00:05:11.377 --> 00:05:14.480
One, I just have to appreciate

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:18.384
what you've done with the show
given the circumstances, man.

00:05:18.384 --> 00:05:22.455
It's been so intimate, and I
know we're talking to each other

00:05:22.455 --> 00:05:25.625
as family and friends
often through this medium,

00:05:25.625 --> 00:05:31.163
but to get to kind of have
these really intimate,

00:05:31.163 --> 00:05:34.333
you know, thoughtful,
still very funny

00:05:34.333 --> 00:05:38.571
but extremely personal
and fulfilling moments

00:05:38.571 --> 00:05:40.640
with you every night
means a lot.

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:43.609
And, you know, you and --
At the beginning.

00:05:43.609 --> 00:05:46.245
And Nancy and Winnie
and Frannie

00:05:46.245 --> 00:05:50.282
getting on and putting
that together was just --

00:05:50.282 --> 00:05:52.284
It was kind of healing
in a way, I got to say.

00:05:52.284 --> 00:05:54.753
So thank you.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:05:54.753 --> 00:05:59.158
I will tell everyone.
My kids love you, man.

00:05:59.158 --> 00:06:00.726
They're obsessed.

00:06:00.726 --> 00:06:03.563
They can't wait to see
"The Little Things."

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:08.700
-[ Laughing ]
-They're so excited.

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:13.339
They love murder whodunit crime
with three --

00:06:13.339 --> 00:06:15.775
By the way, how about --

00:06:15.775 --> 00:06:18.143
Adding to your list
of cool things,

00:06:18.143 --> 00:06:20.179
you get to do a movie
with Denzel Washington.

00:06:20.179 --> 00:06:21.981
-It's one of those moments,
you know --

00:06:21.981 --> 00:06:26.619
I try not to go back to
the trailer to escape the set.

00:06:26.619 --> 00:06:29.588
I'm like, "I'm with Denzel.
Ask him some questions."

00:06:29.588 --> 00:06:31.089
-Anything.
-Ask him some questions.

00:06:31.089 --> 00:06:32.791
And he gets a lot of questions.

00:06:32.791 --> 00:06:36.328
He gets, you know,
the Oscar question a lot.

00:06:36.328 --> 00:06:38.196
Like, "Where do you
keep your Oscar?"

00:06:38.196 --> 00:06:39.898
And he made me laugh.

00:06:39.898 --> 00:06:41.667
He said,
"Next to the other one."

00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:44.536
-[ Laughs ]
-Which I found very amusing.

00:06:44.536 --> 00:06:46.839
-Yeah. That's a great answer.
Oh, man.

00:06:46.839 --> 00:06:48.340
-It was a good one.

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:50.776
-How do we describe the movie?

00:06:50.776 --> 00:06:52.945
-I mean, I can give you
a long-winded answer,

00:06:52.945 --> 00:06:54.246
but you know what it is?

00:06:54.246 --> 00:06:57.983
It's this 1990s
psychological thriller

00:06:57.983 --> 00:07:00.853
that feels like
a throwback movie

00:07:00.853 --> 00:07:04.290
we've kind of been yearning for,
for so many years, right?

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:06.425
We don't see these movies often.

00:07:06.425 --> 00:07:08.795
And it is gripping
to the very last second.

00:07:08.795 --> 00:07:10.896
-It's awesome.
I want to show a clip.

00:07:10.896 --> 00:07:12.932
Here is Rami Malek
and Denzel Washington

00:07:12.932 --> 00:07:16.568
in "The Little Things."
Take a look.

00:07:16.568 --> 00:07:17.936
[ Radio chatter ]

00:07:17.936 --> 00:07:20.573
-Really. This is how
you spend your time off?

00:07:20.573 --> 00:07:22.675
-What do you got?
-Deceased fits the M.O.

00:07:22.675 --> 00:07:24.743
Stab wound, ligature,
killed elsewhere.

00:07:24.743 --> 00:07:27.246
-She a floater?
-Yeah.

00:07:27.246 --> 00:07:29.148
They dumped overflow in here
a few days back.

00:07:29.148 --> 00:07:32.284
Guessing there's mud
in her cavities.

00:07:32.284 --> 00:07:34.787
Shallow grave most likely.

00:07:34.787 --> 00:07:39.758
♪♪

00:07:39.758 --> 00:07:42.661
You ready to tell me
about Mary Roberts?

00:07:42.661 --> 00:07:47.166
♪♪

00:07:47.166 --> 00:07:51.170
Your boy Stan Peters swallowed
a 12-gauge late last night.

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:53.606
♪♪

00:07:53.606 --> 00:07:55.741
-Rami Malek, everybody.
"The Little Things"

00:07:55.741 --> 00:07:58.710
is in theaters this Friday
and available on HBO Max.

00:07:58.710 --> 00:08:01.447
Thanks so much for coming on.
Always great to see you, buddy.

00:08:01.447 --> 00:08:04.350
-It's a pleasure, man.
Thank you for everything.

